{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian","id":1521369,"title":"Why is VTM considered by many to be Judeo-Christian?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-25T04:37:44-07:00","id":1521369,"title":"Why is VTM considered by many to be Judeo-Christian?","content":"While Judaism and Christianity have similarities, I have found that VTM leans more into Christianity, while touching upon other religions and beliefs.<br /> <br /> I am not too well versed in Judaism by any means, so I could be completely wrong.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T04:59:02-07:00","id":1521372,"title":"","content":"Actually i tend to find is more Judaic. Lilith doesn't really show up much in christianity and their arnt any messiac elements to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T05:39:13-07:00","id":1521374,"title":"","content":"Well, Christianism is an offshoot of Judaism originally. And most of Vampire the Mascarade focus on the Old Testament (or the Hebraic Bible) far more than the New Testament (the Christian Bible). I mean, Cain is really important in the Old Testament but not so much in the New, since believers of the latter believe that Jesus redeemed the Sins of Mankind, which would work on Cain, I guess.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly an expert in monotheisms, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T06:38:07-07:00","id":1521379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521372#post1521372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually i tend to find is more Judaic. Lilith doesn't really show up much in christianity and their arnt any messiac elements to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Lillith was not given much mention in Christianity, byt from what I understand in Judaism, and I could be wrong, Lillith as a wife of Adam doesent seem to be taken very seriously, with the texts she does show up in as his wife seemingly being contested. Also, wouldnt Golconda, and Saluot be messianic in a way?<br /> <br /> Of course with everything in VTM, theres always conflicting narartive due to different writers and whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:21:03-07:00","id":1521385,"title":"","content":"Since it's using elements from both faiths and such. It's not a big mystery why this game is considered what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:33:28-07:00","id":1521393,"title":"","content":"Vampire: the Masquarede built on Judeo-Christian elements originally, maybe thats why <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> God, Angels, Damnation, Cain, Abel, Adam and Eve, the whole Book of Nod<br /> But important to mention, even the book points that out, <i>this is what the Vampires believes at the moment</i><br /> In the Dark Ages and prior that many vampire belived they are the descendants of <b>Ixion</b><br /> <br /> (Ixion married Dia, a daughter of Deioneus (or Eioneus), and promised his father-in-law a valuable present. However, he did not pay the bride price, so Deioneus stole some of Ixion's horses in retaliation. Ixion concealed his resentment and invited his father-in-law to a feast at Larissa. When Deioneus arrived, Ixion pushed him into a bed of burning coals and wood.<br /> Ixion went mad, defiled by his act; the neighboring princes were so offended by this act of treachery and violation of xenia that they refused to perform the rituals that would cleanse Ixion of his guilt. Thereafter, Ixion lived as an outlaw and was shunned. By killing his father-in-law, <b>Ixion was reckoned the first man guilty of kin-slaying in Greek mythology.</b><br /> This act alone would warrant Ixion a terrible punishment, but Zeus took pity on Ixion and brought him to Olympus and introduced him at the table of the gods. Instead of being grateful, Ixion grew lustful for Hera,<br /> Zeus found out about his intentions and made a cloud in the shape of Hera, which became known as Nephele (from nephos &quot;cloud&quot;) and tricked Ixion into coupling with it. From the union of Ixion and the false-Hera cloud came Imbros or Centauros, who mated with the Magnesian mares on Mount Pelion, engendering the race of Centaurs, who are called the Ixionidae from their descent.<br /> Ixion was expelled from Olympus and blasted with a thunderbolt. Zeus ordered Hermes to bind Ixion to a winged fiery wheel that was always spinning. Therefore, Ixion was bound to a burning solar wheel for all eternity, at first spinning across the heavens, but in later myth transferred to Tartarus)<br /> <br /> And before that...?<br /> <br /> Important to note, Vampire when came out was different - very different - than it ended up in V20 (and later V5) but carried on the strong connection of America - Judeo-Christian America - and that effected the whole line<br /> <br /> Vampires are also not specifically mentioned in the Bible, though it is possible to interpret certain Biblical passages as referring to vampires<br /> The closest is the Alukah - is a feminine Hebrew word that means &quot;horse-leech&quot;, a type of leech with many teeth that feeds on the throats of animals. According to some biblical scholars, alukah can mean &quot;blood-lusting monster&quot; or vampire (Ironically, t is closely associated with Lilith or thought to be her direct descendant)<br /> <br /> Of course Dracula had a great influence on the Game (as liek the Anne Rice novels)<br /> In his novel, Stoker never explicitly explained the process of how Dracula became a vampire. The Count is loosely based on Vlad III Dracula AKA Vlad the Impaler, the 15th-century warrior and Viviode (ruler) of Wallachia and Transylvania who was infamous for impaling thousands of his enemies on long, wooden spikes. Stoker describes his vampire's past life as a &quot;soldier, statesman, and alchemist... He had a mighty brain, a learning beyond compare... there was no branch of knowledge of his time that he did not essay.&quot; Count Dracula is said to have studied alchemy and black magic at the academy of Scholomance in the Carpathian Mountains; the implication is that to stave off death and achieve immortality, the Count used his arcane knowledge to turn himself into a vampire. This adds to how Dracula is atypical among vampires since most vampires in popular culture are sired by another vampire but Stoker's creation seems to have been a self-made creature of the night, and one with special powers other vampires don't possess.<br /> Francis Ford Coppola's 1992 adaptation Bram Stoker's Dracula took the Count's origin to operatic heights: incensed that his wife Elisabeta's soul was denied entry into Heaven because she committed suicide, the warrior-prince Dracula renounced God and declared war on the Almighty with &quot;all the powers of darkness&quot;. So, like in Stoker's novel, Dracula used black magic to turn himself into a vampire but he did it out of 'eternal love' for his bride<br /> <br /> When Demon came out it alligned well with Vampire and reinforced that Judeo-Christian angle<br /> The Time of Judgement even has a scenario involving God returning to pass judgement upon the world. Some vampires are chosen by God to go to an old church where they must remain for 40 nights. During this time they have a chance at redemption, and if they do redeem themselves they leave the church to see the dawn devoid of the curse of undeath and vampirism.<br /> Basically you can make Christianity and other Abrahamic faiths as important to the setting as you want.<br /> <br /> Fun fact:<br /> Days of Fire and Demon the Fallen indicates God 'died' to prevent the collapse of the universe when Caine murdered Abel due to the finite existing with the infinite.<br /> The Avatar of Mage the Ascension may be fragments of God and it may be possible to resurrect her with them somehow...<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:44:09-07:00","id":1521396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian#post1521369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Judaism and Christianity have similarities, I have found that VTM leans more into Christianity, while touching upon other religions and beliefs.<br /> <br /> I am not too well versed in Judaism by any means, so I could be completely wrong.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine is the canonical father of monsters, that's why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:49:27-07:00","id":1521398,"title":"","content":"I actually find VTM to have a lot of Jewish/Hebrew references. In fact so many terms that most people don't even know about come from Hebrew.<br /> I will be honest and say that I barely know anything about Christianity or the Islam, but I do know Judaism (although I am not a professional).<br /> A few examples for terms in VTM that are actually Hebrew/Jewish words: Gehenna, Baal, Molochim, Tophet, Methuselah, Nephilim, Shedim, and a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:20:32-07:00","id":1521410,"title":"","content":"It's considered Judeo-Christian because the term Judeo-Christian has been forced into the vernacular by Christian supremacists that want to delegitimize Judaism as anything other that a precursor to Christianity. It enables cherry picking Jewish elements with no concern for actual Jewish beliefs or practices, while still telling things from a Christian perspective.<br /> <br /> VtM is Christian coded, because the original authors saw religion as a force in society that did more harm than good, so it was subject to the WoD's satire; and they were born and raised in Christian dominated culture so that was the religion to target. It's not a Jewish game, despite some words from Hebrew sprinkled in here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T23:12:28-07:00","id":1521494,"title":"","content":"It's judeo christian because in addition to mythological elements from judaism, it possess many elements from christianity.<br /> <br /> Gehenna for exemple, despite it's jewish name, is clearly reminiscent of the apocalypse from the new testament books, even taking whole concepts from that, like caine ruling his kind for a millenia of darkness, in the same way that jesus is supposed to rules the world for a millenia after the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> In the same way, golconda is a concept far more christian than judaic, the idea of a being fundamentally sinful and damned finding redemption in the eyes of god is a pretty christian concept.<br /> On that saulot has a pretty christ like role.<br /> <br /> In the same way, the demons and infernalists presented across the game are all pretty much based on the christian view of such things, with the baali being pretty much the image of a satanic cult.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T23:21:33-07:00","id":1521495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521410#post1521410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's considered Judeo-Christian because the term Judeo-Christian has been forced into the vernacular by Christian supremacists that want to delegitimize Judaism as anything other that a precursor to Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>From looking at the origin of the terms, it was rather used as a way to either describe early non paulian christians, jews converted to christianity, or like nietzche to describe a continuity between judaist and christian elements. Before being used as a descriptor of culture and religious elements by people like orwell.<br /> <br /> And one can hardly call nietzche and orwell christian supremacists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T20:41:00-07:00","id":1521572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521396#post1521396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caine is the canonical father of monsters, that's why.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the thing where the scary elder monsters of the setting are named outright for having come from the world before Noah's flood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T04:55:59-07:00","id":1521583,"title":"","content":"On reflection I'd go with abrahanic over anything. It doesn't really fit into either of the big three creating a similar dynamic as kindred of the east has with dharmic religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T06:01:51-07:00","id":1521586,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ultimately it's a vampire game, but the gameline has always leaned heavily into basing the explanations off of Christian and Jewish religious beliefs. There are a few clans (like the Setites or the Laibon) with decidedly different origin stories, but they are very much the exceptions. They even made some of these explanations canon in certain Gehenna scenarios, like the one where Cain, Abel and Lilith all make appearances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T08:46:49-07:00","id":1521595,"title":"","content":"Vampire draws heavily from the Old Testament, which is important to Christians, Jews, and Muslims. Judeo-Christian seems like a weird way to refer to it as it excludes Islam. Maybe Abrahamic would be better.<br /> <br /> While Vampire has a lot of Old Testament stuff in it and very little New Testament, it still has more of a Christian feel to it than Jewish - with ideas about damnation that are far closer to Christianity, especially Catholicism, than Judaism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T14:22:34-07:00","id":1521619,"title":"","content":"Well, if you\u2019re going for mass market appeal, using the Abrahamic religion as your foundation nets you familiarity with a bit over 55% of the globe. The next highest is unaffiliated at 15.6% and includes a bunch of people who, while they may not believe in one of the Abrahamic religions likely belongs to a country where those are are least practiced.<br /> <br /> Hinduism is next at 15.2% and Buddism at 6.6%. Everything else combined makes up less than 9%.<br /> <br /> I get the appeal of wanting to go against the cultural consensus, but in terms of providing something familiar enough for the largest possible part of the population to have a familiar starting point; Cain and Abel is easily going to have the largest possible reach.<br /> <br /> From a business standpoint, unless you want to divorce vampires from religion entirely (akin the Underworld\u2019s who are essentially a mutation; ergo work regardless of religious beliefs) or make Dracula your foundation (and even he becomes one via a deal with Satan in the novel), Abrahamic is definitely the best choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T17:27:29-07:00","id":1521631,"title":"","content":"Or just don't give a definitive answer (or make one answer so prominent in both the books and the in-game setting that it's hard to take other options seriously). Requiem does just fine with making multiple options for how vampires came into being plausible as a game element, and sensible for vampires to debate. Even if you know the &quot;real&quot; answer that has been revealed by Rose Bailey in a non-official capacity but represented her interpretation as developer, Requiem vampires are divorced from any real world religion without escaping real world mythology or even the influence of being inspired by Dracula.<br /> <br /> The idea that you need a solid vampire creation myth that forces you to pick 55% of the population over 45% of the population as a target audience isn't really backed up by much.<br /> <br /> There are also religious/mythological concepts that easily translate into religions beyond clades around origin. &quot;Evil spirit beings create vampires,&quot; is something that would be sensible to more like 99% of the world population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T21:24:42-07:00","id":1521645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521631#post1521631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just don't give a definitive answer (or make one answer so prominent in both the books and the in-game setting that it's hard to take other options seriously). Requiem does just fine with making multiple options for how vampires came into being plausible as a game element, and sensible for vampires to debate. Even if you know the &quot;real&quot; answer that has been revealed by Rose Bailey in a non-official capacity but represented her interpretation as developer, Requiem vampires are divorced from any real world religion without escaping real world mythology or even the influence of being inspired by Dracula.<br /> <br /> The idea that you need a solid vampire creation myth that forces you to pick 55% of the population over 45% of the population as a target audience isn't really backed up by much.<br /> <br /> There are also religious/mythological concepts that easily translate into religions beyond clades around origin. &quot;Evil spirit beings create vampires,&quot; is something that would be sensible to more like 99% of the world population.</div> </div> </div> </div>55% might be the total spread, but I think we have to look at the demographic of who's playing the game. From what I saw here and around on the web (highly anecdotal I know) there's a high proportion in the english speaking world (Although I haven't heard of a lot of players mentioning to be from India). I know there's a strong south american community and there's enough players in Europe to have supplements both in German and in French (I myself bought my first Vampire book in French way back when). Knowing this, it makes sense that the emphasis on the Abrahamic religions even in a bastardized form is not an impediment to it's popularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T23:06:24-07:00","id":1521647,"title":"","content":"Eh? WtA and Mage don't lean on Christian themes at all, and they sold lots and lots of books alongside VtM. There's no real indication that making the games specifically Christian themed actually made it a bigger selling product than it would have been with something else. There really isn't much evidence to back up the idea that you need to make TTRPGs that focus on Christian themes to be successful (D&amp;D... most certainly isn't Christian in an direct way even if there are some obvious influences that come from its creators being from a Christian dominated country). <br /> <br /> Despite the fact that the primary TTRPG markets are in Christian majority countries, most explicitly Christian games don't really sell that well. The TTRPGs that involve a large amount of Christian themes and do well in sales and popularity tend to be ones that do more satirizing of Christianity than not. <br /> <br /> There's also the simple truth that you can't really cater to both major (in terms of population) monotheist faiths at the same time. If you make it too far in one direction you start losing interest from the faith relegated to the sidelines, and if you try to compromise you're far more likely to make nobody with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T05:28:56-07:00","id":1521660,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Vampire has Christian elements because the creators wanted to market to Christians. The themes of the game and the general flavor isn't particularly appealing to people who care a lot about Christianity. I'm pretty certain that the Abrahamic vampiric creation myth comes from the fact that the creators grew up in a heavily Christian culture and the Old Testament carries emotional significance to them (and probably you too) and reminds us of ancientness, legends, and spirituality. Using a Biblical origin myth taps into a preexisting culture power that the Bible has and that isn't primarily a marketing decision, but a creative one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:08:05-07:00","id":1521666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521647#post1521647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? WtA and Mage don't lean on Christian themes at all, and they sold lots and lots of books alongside VtM. There's no real indication that making the games specifically Christian themed actually made it a bigger selling product than it would have been with something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember making that point? If it felt like I did, let me rephrase it: I don't think its emphasis on a Old Testament Style creation myth limited its appeal. The weight of it's demographic is not a 55% / 45% split. It was sold predominantly in the Christian majority countries, using a trope (vampirism) that's at least tangently associated with Christianity (who hasn't heard about the crosses and holy water thing). Obviously, nowadays popular culture has replaced a lot of these with different approaches, but in the 90's those were less prevalent.<br /> <br /> For mage, we have had ample imagery of wizards and mages with no religious subtext (and even then, the Celestial Chorus). Tying the entire story on a Christian Myth seems unwaranted, and even a bit off. <br /> <br /> Werewolf, unless I specifically think about the Loup-Garou, I don't think it's that associated with Christianity much (at least in popular culture).<br /> <br /> So I'm not sure uniting those under the same creation theme as Vampire the Masquerade would have made sense, and in those case I do think it would have hurt the line. But I am not privy to the discussions that went on while the lines were being elaborated on, after they came up with the idea of having more type of things to play in the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite the fact that the primary TTRPG markets are in Christian majority countries, most explicitly Christian games don't really sell that well. The TTRPGs that involve a large amount of Christian themes and do well in sales and popularity tend to be ones that do more satirizing of Christianity than not. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> One can argue that using Christianity in a more negative way is akin to satire in it's appeal. God is not kind nor caring, and neither are his angels in this game. They curse, but never undo or modify their curse when they see the harm it inflicts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the simple truth that you can't really cater to both major (in terms of population) monotheist faiths at the same time. If you make it too far in one direction you start losing interest from the faith relegated to the sidelines, and if you try to compromise you're far more likely to make nobody with it. </div> </div> </div>True, and the emphisis is on highly modified Christian themes with a sprinkle of Jewish religious stories (also modified), and passing mention of other religions.<br /> <br /> To summarize: I think that the writer wanted to write something heavily influenced by Christian myths, did it, and it didn't hurt the game since the ideas portrayed worked within the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:56:54-07:00","id":1521673,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of an Enchina Mother of Monsters style origin for vampire for myself, but that was more for the VTR setting then the Vampire The Masquerade game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:34:06-07:00","id":1521679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521647#post1521647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? WtA and Mage don't lean on Christian themes at all, and they sold lots and lots of books alongside VtM. There's no real indication that making the games specifically Christian themed actually made it a bigger selling product than it would have been with something else. There really isn't much evidence to back up the idea that you need to make TTRPGs that focus on Christian themes to be successful (D&amp;D... most certainly isn't Christian in an direct way even if there are some obvious influences that come from its creators being from a Christian dominated country).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Anecdotal evidence at its finest but the Abrahamic leanings of VtM have always off-putted me. I don't like the game telling me &quot;Abrahamic Faith is Right&quot; in an irrefutable way (or at least a way I felt was conveyed as irrefutable)<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean that Abrahamic faith in a problem irl or even in a Vampire Game, of course. The Lancea et Sanctum is an extremely interesting Covenant for a reason after all. But it not holding the monopoly on Truth about the Vampiric Condition goes a long way to give me much needed freedom : perhaps they are right, absolutely wrong or somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> They can even be all three in three different but great campaigns !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T11:27:43-07:00","id":1521683,"title":"","content":"I always thought the whole tie in with religiousness for VtM (and DtF) was mostly a transgressive touch of &quot;the forbidden&quot; to show off how cool and edgy the games were for the time. We were still a bit more square about religion then and the idea of feeding the rebellion of the youth against the ingrained cultural mores of the earlier generation was a good way to get more engagement.<br /> <br /> I think that games like In Nomine and Kult were very much riding a similar way of emancipation from the shackles of Satanic Panic and the changing position of religion in life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T19:02:17-07:00","id":1521714,"title":"","content":"Because vampires as so ego-eccentric, they think the world's most popular-religion is about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T12:37:42-07:00","id":1521767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521679#post1521679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anecdotal evidence at its finest but the Abrahamic leanings of VtM have always off-putted me. I don't like the game telling me &quot;Abrahamic Faith is Right&quot; in an irrefutable way (or at least a way I felt was conveyed as irrefutable)<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean that Abrahamic faith in a problem irl or even in a Vampire Game, of course. The Lancea et Sanctum is an extremely interesting Covenant for a reason after all. But it not holding the monopoly on Truth about the Vampiric Condition goes a long way to give me much needed freedom : perhaps they are right, absolutely wrong or somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> They can even be all three in three different but great campaigns !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, even if you take everyting in the book of nod at face value, it's not so much &quot;abrahamic faith is right&quot; rather than &quot;some part of abrahamic faith is right&quot;.<br /> <br /> If anything, a lot of the book of nod, the erciyes fragments and the testament of the dark mothers paint a cosmology that, if clearly abrahamic in origin, clearly contradict each abrahamic religion's narrative.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T12:45:54-07:00","id":1521768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521369-why-is-vtm-considered-by-many-to-be-judeo-christian?p=1521714#post1521714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because vampires as so ego-eccentric, they think the world's most popular-religion is about them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well, that's not really what they think. Most of the stories of Nod exist in an annexe way to what judaism and christianity says. Kindred don't believe (for the most part) that the stories of exodus, the whole history of israel and it's relation with yahwee or anything about jesus is about them.<br /> <br /> If anything, their legends takes one character out of the bible and make him their progenitor.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> on the other end, even if they did believe christianity was about them (as did believe the cainite heresy), they would have some good reason. They are after all a supernatural phenomenom, present since at least before the dawn of history, with powers making them on par with the heroes and monsters of myth, and a clear hostile relationship to the divine as shown by their aversion to true faith.<br /> <br /> With such background, it wouldn't be egocentrism to see a narrative about powerful beings and sacrifices of blood and think &quot;this is about my species&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the same way as mages may interpret any legends of incarnated god as stories of powerful mages, or wraith interpreting stories of demonic possessions and angelic visitations as the product of puppetry and apparition of heavily moliate wraiths.<br /> <br /> When you're supernatural, it's not that big of a strech to interpret a legend about supernatural things and interpret it according to one's knowledge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:59:00-07:00","id":1521782,"title":"","content":"Remember all the origins of the Kindred have be told and retold so many times and things got lost in translation or intentionally to serve their needs and that The Book Of Nod, Revaltions Of A Dark Mother and Enriyes Fragments shouldn't be taken at face value and be regarded with a certain degree of skeptism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T19:29:25-07:00","id":1521798,"title":"","content":"In-character, the hegemonic vampire myths are pretty much the ones you\u2019d expect to grow out of a predominantly Christian culture. People on the internet often claim that the game makes those myths objectively true, even though it\u2019s been presenting them as myths since the very first edition, and the Book of Nod is obviously meant to be something written by people who grew up in a medieval Christian environment, in an attempt to mythologize their origins in a way they could understand.<br /> <br /> Out-of-character, vampire lore and gothic style lean heavily on Christian elements for its aesthetics and themes, though not to the extent of actually endorsing the content of Christianity. It\u2019s just a visual language people understand by osmosis and also another way to frame power.<br /> <br /> Judaism is largely absent from the picture, as usual, except as filtered through the lens of Christianity and pop culture. Which is a shame, as specifically Jewish takes on the mythos would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 08-31-2023, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T11:14:30-07:00","id":1521824,"title":"","content":"I might add that christanity was/is the major religion in western society and it would make sense that White-Wolf would draw upon that source for there games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}